license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
abstract: >-
  Meshlytics is a command-line tool that builds a literature dataset from PubMed and analyses its topics through
  the Medical Subject Headings (MeSH) assigned to each paper. Every MeSH descriptor is placed at all of its
  positions in the MeSH tree, so topics can be counted, filtered and compared at different levels of the
  hierarchy and followed over time. It retrieves PubMed records for a list of PubMed IDs, for the papers citing
  a set of cohort papers, or for the most cited papers of a journal, and produces MeSH category co-occurrence at
  tree levels 1-3, topic trends, wordclouds, MeSH term, co-author and institution networks, and top journal,
  author and institution summaries.
keywords:
  - "MeSH"
  - "Medical Subject Headings"
  - "PubMed"
  - "bibliometrics"
